    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Diabetic retinopathy is a vascular disorder of the retina resulting from diabetes, damage caused to the microvasculature and to the vasoproliferative response may lead to bleeding in retina, edema and abnormal growth of blood vessels. Though treated effectively, diabetic retinopathy still remains a leading cause for blindness. This presentation describes the epidemiology and progression of the condition from nonproliferative to proliferative stage, their symptoms, diagnosis and treatment procedures-available and upcoming</marc:subfield>
    </marc:datafield>
